<title>UK: Novorossiisk reopens, but berth repairs continue.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk reopens, but berth repairs continue.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main crude export terminal at Novorossiisk in the Black Sea reopened on Tuesday night after two days' closure due to bad weather, a port inspector said.</p>
<p>He said the largest crude loading berth was closed for scheduled repairs and due to reopen on time on December 24. He added that there were two large oil tankers, the Matilda and the Arteaga, on anchor outside the port which would have to wait for the large berth to reopen before they could load.</p>
<p>The other main Russian export terminals in the Baltic and Black Sea were open, the shipper said.</p>
